  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_1d9253ae316446bb81dc3b2222ab62bc",
      "statement": "apps/server reads all of its configuration from the process environment through a single zod schema in apps/server/src/config/env.ts: DATABASE_URL, SUPABASE_URL (validated as a URL), SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, ADMIN_EMAIL and ADMIN_PASSWORD (minimum 6 characters) are required with no defaults; PORT coerces to a positive integer defaulting to 3000; ALLOW_DEV_CREDENTIAL is the string enum \"true\"/\"false\" transformed to a boolean defaulting to false; ADMIN_ORIGINS defaults to \"http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173\"; and MAPBOX_SECRET_TOKEN is the only optional entry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/server/src/config/env.ts#L8-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:18cbaa4e7ededf1af64ddcaee5418deed09d5d3e9ee5b90ea1f8a44b87b41474:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bd55a76f10ac42febe3ba2159f460470",
      "statement": "loadEnv rejects an invalid environment by joining every zod issue into one \"Invalid environment: <path>: <message>\" error and throwing it, and apps/server/src/index.ts calls loadEnv() at module scope before main(), so a missing or malformed variable aborts the process during import rather than through the logged process.exit(1) path that is reserved for a failed app.listen.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/server/src/config/env.ts#L30-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:71637c4bd03296031e3efb6f5ca374c6bca6fa488d319bf1c5bd0afb491a3b9f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/server/src/index.ts#L6-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:06be845e5b22e9cb09f7177b186faaedcbd1ebfb8409d84a8c1fb6974cae0223:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_57a90513c29048a0aee0dc594581fad2",
      "statement": "The .env auto-load guard only calls process.loadEnvFile when process.env.DATABASE_URL is unset and a .env file exists, and both the existence check and the load path are relative to the process working directory instead of the module; an externally supplied DATABASE_URL therefore prevents the file from being read at all, so values that only existed in .env are not back-filled and instead fail validation, and the server must be started from apps/server (as `pnpm --filter server dev` does) for the file to be found.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/server/package.json#L6-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30ad25c442ec172fb3d5ba2575a8293d4196875d29293ee2f59d47e4ef81f395:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/server/src/config/env.ts#L1-L6",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c650378f6d876b0e92fccbbb1ecbea63ca595fb9b72397d25652282220f399e3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ddd9bd2a90c7455499997f16f64bc869",
      "statement": "loadEnv(source = process.env) is a pure, uncached parse whose source is injectable, which lets unit tests pass a literal record, lets the integration helpers build per-test Env objects through envWith({ ...process.env, ...overrides }) for independently configured app instances, and turns the module-scope .env guard into a no-op once a test bootstrap has pre-loaded .env — this is why the schema is coverable without mutating or depending on the real environment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/server/src/config/env.ts#L30-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:71637c4bd03296031e3efb6f5ca374c6bca6fa488d319bf1c5bd0afb491a3b9f:"
